08e99ce0-d6fc-4dd7-b769-cdee0f36a74b-0
00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:24.764
Last year I founded the New Mexico Death
Care Network,

08e99ce0-d6fc-4dd7-b769-cdee0f36a74b-1
00:07:24.764 --> 00:07:29.680
which is a new nonprofit here in our
state that kind of serves 2 purposes.

ca7c27ef-c7d3-4d0a-9d8e-e00b12b6c691-0
00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.814
We're a professional membership
organization that brings together those

ca7c27ef-c7d3-4d0a-9d8e-e00b12b6c691-1
00:07:32.814 --> 00:07:34.120
that work in end of life care.

c38ef49c-07f7-428f-8dc8-e9397acf3910-0
00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:39.534
We offer networking opportunities and
education and things for each other

c38ef49c-07f7-428f-8dc8-e9397acf3910-1
00:07:39.534 --> 00:07:43.085
support there,
but then we offer an opportunity for

c38ef49c-07f7-428f-8dc8-e9397acf3910-2
00:07:43.085 --> 00:07:47.320
community members to find those services
through our website.

b72e6238-733a-48c9-8966-d0b3d2997c59-0
00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:52.810
And then for those that can't afford and
non medical comprehensive end of life

b72e6238-733a-48c9-8966-d0b3d2997c59-1
00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:57.280
support like that of a death doula,
we will actually pay for the provider

b72e6238-733a-48c9-8966-d0b3d2997c59-2
00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.360
directly for those that can't afford the
services.

d8789bda-3b32-4705-97aa-5817720daeec-0
00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.803
So say someone needed a death doula,
they can't afford it,

d8789bda-3b32-4705-97aa-5817720daeec-1
00:08:02.803 --> 00:08:03.880
we pay the doula directly.

f9efeae2-a6cd-4623-883d-a774eb41975c-0
00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:08.351
So we're effectively keeping good
providers in the field while offering

f9efeae2-a6cd-4623-883d-a774eb41975c-1
00:08:08.351 --> 00:08:10.600
services to those that can't afford it.

90f651dc-c0b7-407b-9ff2-f9de114a89a8-0
00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:15.844
And I'm telling you all of this to let
you know that I'm not an outsider looking

90f651dc-c0b7-407b-9ff2-f9de114a89a8-1
00:08:15.844 --> 00:08:20.123
in on this program or on this topic,
that I'm somebody who will likely be

90f651dc-c0b7-407b-9ff2-f9de114a89a8-2
00:08:20.123 --> 00:08:24.229
boots on the ground working alongside
with licensed clinicians helping

90f651dc-c0b7-407b-9ff2-f9de114a89a8-3
00:08:24.229 --> 00:08:25.560
implement this program.

ffa6ae87-b47a-4651-b090-852355cf1690-0
00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.800
And so I think it's important that you
understand a little bit of background

ffa6ae87-b47a-4651-b090-852355cf1690-1
00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.000
about who I am and why I'm talking about
all this.

399c3380-89fa-493f-b8a2-8d733d813acc-0
00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:37.800
So today, what I hope to cover is first,
what's a death doula?

6ce1b017-ab2e-495f-9d75-f5c4ec1881fe-0
00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:41.670
I think many people on this call
understand the role and the scope and the

6ce1b017-ab2e-495f-9d75-f5c4ec1881fe-1
00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:45.500
distinction of death doulas from clinical
care, but I doubt everyone does,

6ce1b017-ab2e-495f-9d75-f5c4ec1881fe-2
00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.360
and maybe some who listen to the
recording later won't.

fac88948-9034-4473-a02c-68ee6e3dcf7f-0
00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.120
So I want to make sure we cover that
first.

2f180bde-51b9-4fd9-9f3d-d53586714446-0
00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:54.790
And then I want to cover the case for
death doulas being included in SB 219 in

2f180bde-51b9-4fd9-9f3d-d53586714446-1
00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:56.560
the implementation of the program.

fe3365c7-f2d9-44fd-ae34-4e930f4fbe7d-0
00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:01.560
Why psilocybin needs continuity providers
such as death doulas?

5f2ddad2-4f33-4754-9805-8a48be5addca-0
00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:06.920
I'll also offer kind of a model of care
like the doula continuum.

323e4205-d136-40ac-85b2-2f9637e11a52-0
00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:13.573
It's something that very much mirrors how
doulas work with folks at end of life and

323e4205-d136-40ac-85b2-2f9637e11a52-1
00:09:13.573 --> 00:09:18.453
how that can kind of seamlessly weave
into the arc of care throughout a

323e4205-d136-40ac-85b2-2f9637e11a52-2
00:09:18.453 --> 00:09:22.520
psilocybin preparation, dosing,
and integration experience.

df92f8fe-bebd-4517-8841-cdc55cd187c1-0
00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:28.046
And then there's some kind of hard
questions that I think are really

df92f8fe-bebd-4517-8841-cdc55cd187c1-1
00:09:28.046 --> 00:09:32.252
important to acknowledge and talk about
specifically scope, licensure,

df92f8fe-bebd-4517-8841-cdc55cd187c1-2
00:09:32.252 --> 00:09:37.109
liability and safety surrounding bringing
in additional supportive roles that are

df92f8fe-bebd-4517-8841-cdc55cd187c1-3
00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:39.360
unlicensed like that of a death doula.

f0de93cc-f65b-4e1a-b48b-f3e44935fc3e-0
00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:44.032
And then some practical considerations
that I'd like us to kind of chat about

f0de93cc-f65b-4e1a-b48b-f3e44935fc3e-1
00:09:44.032 --> 00:09:48.144
today and maybe questions we can bounce
back and forth and things to continue

f0de93cc-f65b-4e1a-b48b-f3e44935fc3e-2
00:09:48.144 --> 00:09:50.200
kind of noodling on as we move forward.

f7509981-39f8-4cba-b6d9-6dea8b3bad1d-0
00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:58.080
So first I want to acknowledge that this
is not anything new.

f410cd36-06b3-42f8-bdb5-2915448be4d1-0
00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:01.149
Not everybody is familiar with death
doulas,

f410cd36-06b3-42f8-bdb5-2915448be4d1-1
00:10:01.149 --> 00:10:06.281
but this is an ancient tradition and this
is just the modern resurgence and kind of

f410cd36-06b3-42f8-bdb5-2915448be4d1-2
00:10:06.281 --> 00:10:09.520
the modern iteration of it as becoming a
profession.

5ded9bf9-e2df-4c47-b484-e184905f1fad-0
00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.960
Indigenous cultures have held positions
such as a death doula forever, right?

e8119fef-1c4b-40ef-b0ef-f75d20c80dba-0
00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:21.098
Medicine people, elders, wisdom keepers,
kid and dead as shamans,

e8119fef-1c4b-40ef-b0ef-f75d20c80dba-1
00:10:21.098 --> 00:10:24.680
all every kind of iteration of this
possible.

bcd1ffd5-8625-437a-b40d-15d6402b2c28-0
00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:31.397
The word doula itself is ancient Greek
and it means a woman who helps or serves,

bcd1ffd5-8625-437a-b40d-15d6402b2c28-1
00:10:31.397 --> 00:10:33.560
or one who mothers the mother.

d971a0c5-a72f-4c2d-8deb-3b6552bf7c98-0
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:39.682
So very often you hear about doulas in
terms of birth or lactation or postpartum

d971a0c5-a72f-4c2d-8deb-3b6552bf7c98-1
00:10:39.682 --> 00:10:44.524
doulas and death Doulas use the same
title because there are so many

d971a0c5-a72f-4c2d-8deb-3b6552bf7c98-2
00:10:44.524 --> 00:10:47.120
similarities between birth and death.

9e05876a-f5d2-4fb3-b299-e5a8db143f6f-0
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:54.331
The way I like to explain it is that all
of the work and the effort and the pain

9e05876a-f5d2-4fb3-b299-e5a8db143f6f-1
00:10:54.331 --> 00:11:00.000
of labouring life into the world falls on
our mothers on our way out of the world.

69f947e5-c50c-4b02-8d06-e9e3b6d27635-0
00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.680
All of that work and that effort,
that labor process falls on us.

fdfda2ef-2328-4142-8874-861e0fc40189-0
00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:08.948
And so very often the same work and prep,
preparation, excuse me,

fdfda2ef-2328-4142-8874-861e0fc40189-1
00:11:08.948 --> 00:11:14.482
that you want to offer for a woman doing
the hard work of bringing life into the

fdfda2ef-2328-4142-8874-861e0fc40189-2
00:11:14.482 --> 00:11:20.152
world is the same type of preparation and,
and environment that you want to create

fdfda2ef-2328-4142-8874-861e0fc40189-3
00:11:20.152 --> 00:11:24.319
for a person who's doing the hard work of
leaving the world.

0e50c1e7-33e2-4a5f-8521-7b90041dae81-0
00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:28.360
And so doulas work in kind of multiple
areas.

306e42a5-e76d-4054-981f-d3066276bce3-0
00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:31.774
Emotionally,
we're helping people hold grief and fear

306e42a5-e76d-4054-981f-d3066276bce3-1
00:11:31.774 --> 00:11:33.560
and process anticipatory loss.

c9f27e12-4caa-4544-9f43-58b31ce065fa-0
00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:36.320
Existentially.

b53aad33-e1d1-4083-be55-d5314f8c1398-0
00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.760
It's it's talking with clients about life
reviews, right?

3ffa948a-a6e4-42c2-9f5c-6457ca5a7f53-0
00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.600
What's the theme of your life story?

7d165889-733d-438b-b2e3-9ec20dde8e12-0
00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:47.109
What is all of this been about and how
can we maybe document it through

7d165889-733d-438b-b2e3-9ec20dde8e12-1
00:11:47.109 --> 00:11:52.926
something like a legacy project or
letters to your loved ones Relationally,

7d165889-733d-438b-b2e3-9ec20dde8e12-2
00:11:52.926 --> 00:11:58.665
families preparing for folks stopping
treatment or maybe entering Hospice,

7d165889-733d-438b-b2e3-9ec20dde8e12-3
00:11:58.665 --> 00:12:04.711
having difficult conversations amongst
family members where maybe values don't

7d165889-733d-438b-b2e3-9ec20dde8e12-4
00:12:04.711 --> 00:12:05.400
match up.

8cd0fa10-0930-43ea-997c-10c1c0028dbc-0
00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:08.674
That's a lot of what doulas do,
advocating for our client,

8cd0fa10-0930-43ea-997c-10c1c0028dbc-1
00:12:08.674 --> 00:12:12.686
the person who is dying and making sure
that their wishes are heard amongst

8cd0fa10-0930-43ea-997c-10c1c0028dbc-2
00:12:12.686 --> 00:12:15.959
everyone in the family or in their system,
their care circle.

3a4593ec-b997-4e4b-a45e-4eef0afc6528-0
00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:20.632
And practically,
it's a lot of helping navigate through

3a4593ec-b997-4e4b-a45e-4eef0afc6528-1
00:12:20.632 --> 00:12:23.480
the entire process and journey of end of
life.

e58bec56-d421-4fe9-9b07-2ae76e931af9-0
00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:27.000
Making sure that the paperwork is done.

e3c693eb-ed74-4a7b-a546-dd606f67f786-0
00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:31.344
You know, all of the boxes are checked,
what I call the business of death that

e3c693eb-ed74-4a7b-a546-dd606f67f786-1
00:12:31.344 --> 00:12:34.553
your advance directives, your most,
your will, your trusts,

e3c693eb-ed74-4a7b-a546-dd606f67f786-2
00:12:34.553 --> 00:12:37.119
your beneficiaries and transfer on death
forms.

0ffd1e51-e778-4598-9591-728066dbfb3a-0
00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:43.600
All of those things are taken care of and
the after plans as well, right?

613197ba-af85-4824-98dc-b7cc42a6c0b1-0
00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:45.400
What do you want to happen to your dead
body?

d5b583ac-c578-47a4-89e6-137db39a2861-0
00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:47.240
How do you plan for your memorial?

883d9e67-3afe-43f9-b7e4-c5a9a0f1ed54-0
00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:51.057
What ways can we honor you that are
unique and important and important to you

883d9e67-3afe-43f9-b7e4-c5a9a0f1ed54-1
00:12:51.057 --> 00:12:51.840
and your family?

83e5dc4d-a8aa-4e28-9384-8e4359aadfaf-0
00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:55.760
And so doulas kind of work in all of
those areas.

9f9c8bd4-ba9b-4bd6-a85b-64caec34d169-0
00:12:56.040 --> 00:13:01.672
And there's often a lot of overlap
between clinical roles or between Hospice

9f9c8bd4-ba9b-4bd6-a85b-64caec34d169-1
00:13:01.672 --> 00:13:03.720
roles and what a doula does.

06017fb1-ea3a-477a-b966-cf0483f2abe6-0
00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.960
A doula does some of the things that a
social worker might do.

97574aee-e621-4392-bbff-177755d0cf46-0
00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:10.528
They have some of the spiritual
conversations that a chaplain or

97574aee-e621-4392-bbff-177755d0cf46-1
00:13:10.528 --> 00:13:11.960
spiritual advisor might have.

9bb0900b-a6ea-4d80-9a20-fb22f4dd1588-0
00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:16.916
Sometimes a doula will sit and offer some
respite care so that the loved one can go

9bb0900b-a6ea-4d80-9a20-fb22f4dd1588-1
00:13:16.916 --> 00:13:20.734
out and go to the grocery store,
similar to what a Hospice volunteer might

9bb0900b-a6ea-4d80-9a20-fb22f4dd1588-2
00:13:20.734 --> 00:13:21.039
offer.

1bf9311a-f8dd-40ae-8f8e-6d46101b40c4-0
00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:23.960
And so there's lots of overlap there.

00eba63e-e91f-4c9d-816b-f37b7f072883-0
00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:28.846
And I think the distinction is that
doulas are the same, the same face,

00eba63e-e91f-4c9d-816b-f37b7f072883-1
00:13:28.846 --> 00:13:34.004
the same continuous person through the
entire journey with the client and a

00eba63e-e91f-4c9d-816b-f37b7f072883-2
00:13:34.004 --> 00:13:34.480
family.

4334ebd5-bf16-4a67-a813-cd92648801d7-0
00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:41.514
And that's really important to those who
are going through such a scary and

4334ebd5-bf16-4a67-a813-cd92648801d7-1
00:13:41.514 --> 00:13:42.560
profound time.

89dad35e-f3dd-499e-97cf-620187deb300-0
00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:50.000
So it's important to note that doulas are
not clinicians.

7127438e-a138-4883-a7a1-7c0d76035604-0
00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.883
And when I say clinician,
I'm not just talking about physicians,

7127438e-a138-4883-a7a1-7c0d76035604-1
00:13:52.883 --> 00:13:54.880
I'm talking about any licensed
practitioner.

8d5d5a8c-125e-4151-8d26-2f1fa6f7518f-0
00:13:55.120 --> 00:14:01.018
So social workers, therapists, counselors,
nurses, physicians, nurse practitioners,

8d5d5a8c-125e-4151-8d26-2f1fa6f7518f-1
00:14:01.018 --> 00:14:04.880
P as everybody in between, right,
licensed clinicians.

20186f01-7eec-43f0-aec5-acf382babd90-0
00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:09.160
So we are not that we are continuity
providers.

926150dd-8a44-4691-9605-01112661b6f5-0
00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:14.545
So we hold the whole arc of before,
during and after a clinical intervention

926150dd-8a44-4691-9605-01112661b6f5-1
00:14:14.545 --> 00:14:17.440
or before, during and after a death,
right?

913fde2e-6077-41d7-a33c-110acd91b600-0
00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:20.369
The preparation,
the actual vigil time and then grief

913fde2e-6077-41d7-a33c-110acd91b600-1
00:14:20.369 --> 00:14:21.400
support afterwards.

5ffb4cc7-96b9-4b52-8a6e-3908a565d3a8-0
00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:26.913
So doulas are kind of prime to be that
continuity piece throughout a,

5ffb4cc7-96b9-4b52-8a6e-3908a565d3a8-1
00:14:26.913 --> 00:14:30.200
a medicine or psilocybin experience as
well.

a59ac169-32fe-4ef7-8c74-37a515bf976e-0
00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:37.320
So the licensed clinician is primarily
there for episodic care, right?

6cf8eaba-108f-43a8-99ea-0aea300891e3-0
00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:40.390
There's preparation sessions,
the dosing session,

6cf8eaba-108f-43a8-99ea-0aea300891e3-1
00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:45.120
integration sessions where the doula
would may be there for continuous care.

a406fa4f-e9f0-459b-94b5-59dc67234d4e-0
00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:49.196
I've had clients that I've worked with
for 18 months before they passed away,

a406fa4f-e9f0-459b-94b5-59dc67234d4e-1
00:14:49.196 --> 00:14:53.356
seeing them weekly for a couple of hours
a week and that time actually increasing

a406fa4f-e9f0-459b-94b5-59dc67234d4e-2
00:14:53.356 --> 00:14:56.400
and then actually being there through the
the death itself.

f1a1ef5f-8aa3-42f6-ab5c-88eded90e925-0
00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:03.381
A clinician may be focused specifically
on the psilocybin experience and what

f1a1ef5f-8aa3-42f6-ab5c-88eded90e925-1
00:15:03.381 --> 00:15:07.960
that may offer as a clinical intervention
for an end of life patient.

ce0d2e4b-2d71-42cd-bc13-889dfb8e85e3-0
00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:13.218
Where the doula will be focused on the
entire end of life journey of not just

ce0d2e4b-2d71-42cd-bc13-889dfb8e85e3-1
00:15:13.218 --> 00:15:15.640
the person dying but their family as well.

060cc373-59d0-46c5-92cb-d2a0997fcf2c-0
00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:21.896
The licensed clinician is primarily there
with clinical responsibility and they

060cc373-59d0-46c5-92cb-d2a0997fcf2c-1
00:15:21.896 --> 00:15:23.000
hold that liability.

0753852c-9766-459c-a6ad-fd7dab42770c-0
00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:27.380
Where the doula is there more
relationally working more on existential

0753852c-9766-459c-a6ad-fd7dab42770c-1
00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:31.154
and psychosocial support,
The licensed clinician will be bound by

0753852c-9766-459c-a6ad-fd7dab42770c-2
00:15:31.154 --> 00:15:35.672
the program structure and Department of
Health rules as well as their scope of

0753852c-9766-459c-a6ad-fd7dab42770c-3
00:15:35.672 --> 00:15:37.960
practice legally within their licensure.

d34b70fd-dfcf-4f86-89e0-dab26294b94b-0
00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:43.560
And a doula's got a more flexible home
community based presence.

ce9381fa-0cac-4402-bcb1-a7f9f605f609-0
00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:49.863
It's kind of a a paid friend, if you will,
someone to be there through the entire

ce9381fa-0cac-4402-bcb1-a7f9f605f609-1
00:15:49.863 --> 00:15:51.920
arc of the journey with you.

1a07afa4-3aa3-4e69-919a-39678fa32195-0
00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:57.345
And obviously a licensed clinician has
got their medical or psychological

1a07afa4-3aa3-4e69-919a-39678fa32195-1
00:15:57.345 --> 00:16:02.604
training requirements and we need to kind
of talk about what the requirements may

1a07afa4-3aa3-4e69-919a-39678fa32195-2
00:16:02.604 --> 00:16:04.400
be for a doula in this role.

