00:24:48.320 --> 00:24:51.920
And really important is the cultural and
spiritual context setting.

c68de98c-65a2-4cce-8d5a-b7b0de158a68-0
00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:57.044
Jen talked about this a ton last time and
I think that's, that's absolutely key,

c68de98c-65a2-4cce-8d5a-b7b0de158a68-1
00:24:57.044 --> 00:24:59.600
especially in the end of life space for
folks.

01c9026a-c7cf-4687-a95c-7704436273dd-0
00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:04.618
So as far as the policy goes,
this is important because it'll help

01c9026a-c7cf-4687-a95c-7704436273dd-1
00:25:04.618 --> 00:25:08.800
improve safety and reduce risk of
distress during the sessions.

584f19be-a3cb-44ba-8b7d-77a2dc63f88d-0
00:25:09.120 --> 00:25:12.450
Because again,
there's been this continuous person that

584f19be-a3cb-44ba-8b7d-77a2dc63f88d-1
00:25:12.450 --> 00:25:17.386
has helped them walk through all of this
prep beyond just that one or two sessions

584f19be-a3cb-44ba-8b7d-77a2dc63f88d-2
00:25:17.386 --> 00:25:20.360
that may be covered under the the program
itself.

2a2046b6-ab29-4459-852c-66fef93256ab-0
00:25:22.600 --> 00:25:28.300
And it extends beyond what clinicians
actually have time and bandwidth for,

2a2046b6-ab29-4459-852c-66fef93256ab-1
00:25:28.300 --> 00:25:33.850
just like all parts of our medical system,
palliative care, Hospice care,

2a2046b6-ab29-4459-852c-66fef93256ab-2
00:25:33.850 --> 00:25:39.775
that those medical teams are stretched
incredibly thin and they don't have the

2a2046b6-ab29-4459-852c-66fef93256ab-3
00:25:39.775 --> 00:25:45.775
the space to see clients for extended
long preparation and integration sessions

2a2046b6-ab29-4459-852c-66fef93256ab-4
00:25:45.775 --> 00:25:47.800
before and after a journey.

2b4629f6-220b-4ae5-b260-4d73e32ca161-0
00:25:48.680 --> 00:25:53.842
And so we can also kind of help the eyes
and ears to help the clinical team assess

2b4629f6-220b-4ae5-b260-4d73e32ca161-1
00:25:53.842 --> 00:25:57.139
cultural gaps,
things that we may be missing because

2b4629f6-220b-4ae5-b260-4d73e32ca161-2
00:25:57.139 --> 00:26:00.187
again,
the clinicians and the medical team don't

2b4629f6-220b-4ae5-b260-4d73e32ca161-3
00:26:00.187 --> 00:26:02.800
have the time to spend that a doula might.

6d321578-8106-46f1-8e4b-cf0716b110bc-0
00:26:03.360 --> 00:26:07.040
And then this reduces the burden on
licensed facilitators and clinicians.

f98dc60b-45cd-46d2-b60e-ebe7d48b137d-0
00:26:07.400 --> 00:26:13.328
So if doulas are working alongside
licensed clinicians that that combination

f98dc60b-45cd-46d2-b60e-ebe7d48b137d-1
00:26:13.328 --> 00:26:19.796
can offer so much more to a patient and a
family than just the the clinical process

f98dc60b-45cd-46d2-b60e-ebe7d48b137d-2
00:26:19.796 --> 00:26:20.720
of medicine.

021bca1a-4005-4eb7-8ab0-739c06f26ada-0
00:26:23.480 --> 00:26:26.920
And so I think integration again is where
doulas can be the most essential.

ddea32e4-c407-4961-aaf6-3e7fdc12268b-0
00:26:28.440 --> 00:26:32.004
If we only treat this as a clinical
intervention,

ddea32e4-c407-4961-aaf6-3e7fdc12268b-1
00:26:32.004 --> 00:26:37.850
it will be effective and we will miss out
on a lot of opportunity for the patient

ddea32e4-c407-4961-aaf6-3e7fdc12268b-2
00:26:37.850 --> 00:26:38.920
and the family.

b8b63ae0-9691-4921-a48a-70d8299fc980-0
00:26:40.960 --> 00:26:45.592
Without long term integration,
the insights may not translate into

b8b63ae0-9691-4921-a48a-70d8299fc980-1
00:26:45.592 --> 00:26:46.560
actual action.

5d79df84-8c5e-4a8b-a494-403e77ee3d73-0
00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:50.431
And so where doulas can do is help,
like we said earlier,

5d79df84-8c5e-4a8b-a494-403e77ee3d73-1
00:26:50.431 --> 00:26:54.875
actually move things into real life
concrete actions that make a difference

5d79df84-8c5e-4a8b-a494-403e77ee3d73-2
00:26:54.875 --> 00:26:58.442
in how they not only live the rest of the
time they're here,

5d79df84-8c5e-4a8b-a494-403e77ee3d73-3
00:26:58.442 --> 00:27:03.236
but what their death looks like and how
their family ends up processing the grief

5d79df84-8c5e-4a8b-a494-403e77ee3d73-4
00:27:03.236 --> 00:27:03.880
afterwards.

fee62ec2-0efc-444b-b2ba-55c86f7943b0-0
00:27:04.480 --> 00:27:09.320
So the key distinctions from clinicians
where we're translating insights into end

fee62ec2-0efc-444b-b2ba-55c86f7943b0-1
00:27:09.320 --> 00:27:12.330
of life decisions,
it's not just the psychological

fee62ec2-0efc-444b-b2ba-55c86f7943b0-2
00:27:12.330 --> 00:27:14.160
processing, it's the real life.

85bef8c0-3bc3-4492-b974-53db35b7150e-0
00:27:15.880 --> 00:27:16.120
Yeah.

347dd799-5baf-4536-b20c-ffcaef5c9769-0
00:27:16.120 --> 00:27:19.328
I keep saying it,
but the real life concrete actions the

347dd799-5baf-4536-b20c-ffcaef5c9769-1
00:27:19.328 --> 00:27:23.718
world can also help support repair of
relationships and that presence extends

347dd799-5baf-4536-b20c-ffcaef5c9769-2
00:27:23.718 --> 00:27:25.520
to active death and bereavement.

b37052fb-6e37-4643-a7a9-9d286c1027f0-0
00:27:27.080 --> 00:27:31.293
We're holding those legacy projects
through to completion so that they're

b37052fb-6e37-4643-a7a9-9d286c1027f0-1
00:27:31.293 --> 00:27:35.280
actually delivered to family members
before or after the person dies.

5f5a865b-c404-4241-abc3-e823ecf1e4ce-0
00:27:37.240 --> 00:27:38.840
It is non clinical.

2f2f4c1b-c840-40c2-b83a-dc93102b0876-0
00:27:39.080 --> 00:27:42.600
We are not diagnosing,
We are not treating it as non directive.

aaad2639-2178-4a2d-8f69-6fcda07a3b82-0
00:27:44.560 --> 00:27:48.040
We help bridge the mystical experience
into practical life closure.

1838aa7c-8b8d-4d5d-a839-99f5246b21d4-0
00:27:48.400 --> 00:27:51.400
And so again,
it's relationship based over time.

7bb0e027-f645-456a-a750-991dc73d2ad5-0
00:27:51.680 --> 00:27:53.120
It's not episodic.

bd4f559f-dd79-40d7-8d37-62bc9e192630-0
00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:56.120
So it's not just coming in for a clinical
intervention.

c89749f4-5ec3-416e-a7b3-de0452824bc3-0
00:27:56.120 --> 00:27:59.240
It's continuing throughout the entire arc
of care.

3989b4d1-93d8-416e-a993-c4dcde3d339b-0
00:28:01.400 --> 00:28:06.871
Another big thing to talk about is that
especially here in New Mexico,

3989b4d1-93d8-416e-a993-c4dcde3d339b-1
00:28:06.871 --> 00:28:12.419
we've got a very large rural population,
a large indigenous population,

3989b4d1-93d8-416e-a993-c4dcde3d339b-2
00:28:12.419 --> 00:28:15.040
and a large low income population.

a60655bd-e3d0-4b22-b06d-23570cfbcc8a-0
00:28:15.320 --> 00:28:17.840
So doulas can help extend the reach of
the program.

272ec1bd-23aa-42fd-a6b1-815094b4629a-0
00:28:19.920 --> 00:28:24.636
Excluding doulas risks creating a program
that's clinically sound and socially

272ec1bd-23aa-42fd-a6b1-815094b4629a-1
00:28:24.636 --> 00:28:27.800
unacceptable or inaccessible,
which is unacceptable.

55dfa046-5596-49a2-ac7a-aec916d0bbe2-0
00:28:27.920 --> 00:28:29.200
That was a Freudian slip.

035c94bd-c352-4a60-b0d0-982d9366176e-0
00:28:31.040 --> 00:28:35.135
It's always been a big challenge to me
that even doula work is something that

035c94bd-c352-4a60-b0d0-982d9366176e-1
00:28:35.135 --> 00:28:39.440
very quickly could become only available
to a small percentage of the population.

2afd3a84-45ac-4dfa-be42-edc43a82abb0-0
00:28:39.840 --> 00:28:44.651
And I think all of us in this room are
really aware of the fact that psychedelic

2afd3a84-45ac-4dfa-be42-edc43a82abb0-1
00:28:44.651 --> 00:28:49.344
work and psilocybin work is very quickly
kind of becoming another one of those

2afd3a84-45ac-4dfa-be42-edc43a82abb0-2
00:28:49.344 --> 00:28:49.760
things.

b50ad44f-b465-4782-a6e8-2dcbd131a308-0
00:28:50.120 --> 00:28:53.480
So bringing doulas in can kind of help
